  "answer": "I'll look through the Shopizer storefront cart API and how store merchant configuration is read so the line-quantity limit can be applied without a restart.The cart writes go through one facade. I'll enforce the per-store maximum there, before anything is saved, and read the setting on each request.The storefront cart API now rejects any create, add, or quantity change that would put more than N units on one line. N comes from the store merchant configuration key `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` and is read on each request (default 99 when it is missing or not a whole number). A quantity of 0 still removes the line. Over-limit requests return HTTP 400 and the cart is not saved.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 responses and that the cart is unchanged, because the cart integration tests need a running Shopizer application and database\"], \"missing\": [\"a fixture or documented step to set CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and call POST /api/v1/cart, PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}, and POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi\"]}",
